1
00:00:02,679 --> 00:00:09,000
The next day was foggy. Everything on the farm was dripping wet. The grass

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:16,359
looked like a magic carpet. The asparagus patch looked like a silver forest.

3
00:00:16,359 --> 00:00:23,000
On foggy mornings, Charlotte's web was truly a thing of beauty.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,439
This morning, each thin strand was decorated with dozens of tiny beads of

5
00:00:28,439 --> 00:00:34,198
water. The web glistened in the light and made a pattern of loveliness and

6
00:00:34,198 --> 00:00:39,880
mystery like a delicate veil. Even Lurvy, who wasn't particularly

7
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:46,198
interested in beauty, noticed the web when he came with the pig's breakfast.

8
00:00:46,198 --> 00:00:51,639
He noted how clearly it showed up, and he noted how big and carefully built it

9
00:00:51,639 --> 00:00:57,479
was. And then he took another look, and he saw something that made him set his

10
00:00:57,479 --> 00:01:05,399
pale down. There in the center of the web, neatly woven in block letters, was

11
00:01:05,399 --> 00:01:13,719
a message. It said, "Some pig."

12
00:01:13,719 --> 00:01:19,960
Lurvy felt weak. He brushed his hand across his eyes and stared harder at

13
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:26,679
Charlotte's Web. "I'm saying things," he whispered. He dropped to his knees and

14
00:01:26,679 --> 00:01:32,279
uttered a short prayer. Then forgetting all about Wilbur's breakfast, he walked

15
00:01:32,279 --> 00:01:34,118
back to the house and called Mr.

16
00:01:34,118 --> 00:01:41,639
Zuckerman. I think you'd better come down to the pig pan, he said.

17
00:01:41,639 --> 00:01:44,840
What's the trouble? asked Mr. Zuckerman.

18
00:01:44,840 --> 00:01:47,800
Anything wrong with the pig?

19
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:53,880
Not exactly, said Lurvy. Come and see for yourself.

20
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:59,319
The two men walked silently down to Wilbur's yard. Lurvy pointed to the

21
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:03,238
spider's web. "Do you see what I see?"

22
00:02:03,238 --> 00:02:12,760
he asked. Zuckerman stared at the writing on the web. Then he murmured the words, "Some pig."

23
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:19,520
Then he looked at Lurvy. Then they both began to tremble.

24
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:26,198
Charlotte, sleepy after her night's exertions, smiled as she watched. Wilbur

25
00:02:26,198 --> 00:02:28,920
came and stood directly under the web.

26
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:37,960
"Some pig!" muttered Lurvy in a low voice. "Some pig!" whispered Mr.

27
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:47,238
Zuckerman. They stared and stared for a long time at Wilbur. Then they stared at Charlotte.

28
00:02:47,238 --> 00:02:50,679
"You don't suppose that that spider?"

29
00:02:50,679 --> 00:02:55,719
began Mr. Zuckerman, but he shook his head and didn't finish the sentence.

30
00:02:55,719 --> 00:03:02,359
Instead, he walked solemnly back up to the house and spoke to his wife. "Edith,

31
00:03:02,359 --> 00:03:07,880
something has happened," he said in a weak voice. He went into the living room

32
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:12,920
and sat down, and Mrs. Zuckerman followed.

33
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:19,399
"I've got something to tell you, Edith," he said. "You better sit down." Mrs.

34
00:03:19,399 --> 00:03:25,639
Zuckerman sank into a chair. She looked pale and frightened. "Edith," he said,

35
00:03:25,639 --> 00:03:31,158
trying to keep his voice steady. "I think you had best be told that uh we

36
00:03:31,158 --> 00:03:38,039
have a very unusual pig." A look of complete bewilderment came over Mrs.

37
00:03:38,039 --> 00:03:48,039
Zuckerman's face. "Homer Zuckerman, what in the world are you talking about?" she said.

38
00:03:48,039 --> 00:03:54,439
This is a very serious thing, Edith," he replied. "Our pig is completely out of

39
00:03:54,439 --> 00:04:00,840
the ordinary." "What's unusual about the pig?" asked Mrs. Zuckerman, who was

40
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:03,560
beginning to recover from her scare.

41
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:10,600
"Well, I don't really know yet," said Mr. Zuckerman. "But we have received a

42
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:18,600
sign, Edith. A mysterious sign. A miracle has happened on this farm.

43
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:22,920
There was a large spider's web in the doorway of the barn cellar, right over

44
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:28,279
the pig pin. And when Larvy went to feed the pig this morning, he noticed the web

45
00:04:28,279 --> 00:04:32,920
cuz it was foggy. And you know how a spider's web looks very distinct in a

46
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:41,399
fog. And right spang in the middle of the web, there were the words some pig.

47
00:04:41,399 --> 00:04:46,198
The words were woven right into the web.

48
00:04:46,198 --> 00:04:50,920
They were actually part of the web, Edith. I know because I have been down

49
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:58,439
there and seen them. It says, "Some pig just as clear as clear can be. There can

50
00:04:58,439 --> 00:05:03,800
be no mistake about it. A miracle has happened and a sign has occurred here on

51
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:11,800
Earth right on our farm, and we have no ordinary pig." "Well," said Mrs.

52
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:21,399
Zuckerman, it seems to me you're a little off. It seems to me we have no ordinary spider.

53
00:05:21,399 --> 00:05:27,238
Oh no, said Zuckerman. It's the pig that's unusual. It says so right there

54
00:05:27,238 --> 00:05:33,639
in the middle of the web. Maybe so, said Mrs. Zuckerman. Just the same, I intend

55
00:05:33,639 --> 00:05:39,639
to have a look at that spider. It's just a common gray spider, said Zuckerman.

56
00:05:39,639 --> 00:05:44,359
They got up and together they walked down to Wilbur's yard. You see, Edith,

57
00:05:44,359 --> 00:05:48,520
it's just a common gray spatter.

58
00:05:48,520 --> 00:05:53,560
Wilbur was pleased to receive so much attention. Lurvy was still standing

59
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:59,639
there, and Mr. and Mrs. Zuckerman, all three, stood for about an hour reading

60
00:05:59,639 --> 00:06:04,920
the words on the web over and over and watching Wilbur.

61
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:10,039
Charlotte was delighted with the way her trick was working. She sat without

62
00:06:10,039 --> 00:06:15,639
moving a muscle and listened to the conversation of the people.

63
00:06:15,639 --> 00:06:21,000
When a small fly blundered into the web just beyond the word pig, Charlotte

64
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:26,840
dropped quickly down, rolled the fly up, and carried it out of the way. After a

65
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:32,359
while, the fog lifted, the web dried off, and the words didn't show up so

66
00:06:32,359 --> 00:06:37,880
plainly. The Zuckerman's and Lurvy walked back to the house. Just before

67
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:44,920
they left the pig pin, Mr. Zuckerman took one last look at Wilbur.

68
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:49,319
You know, he said in an important voice.

69
00:06:49,319 --> 00:06:55,639
I've thought all along that that pig of ours was an extra good one. He's a solid

70
00:06:55,639 --> 00:06:59,719
pig. That pig is as solid as they come.

71
00:06:59,719 --> 00:07:06,679
You notice how solid he is around the shoulders, Lurvy? Sure, sure I do, said

72
00:07:06,679 --> 00:07:10,599
Lurvy. I've always noticed that pig.

73
00:07:10,599 --> 00:07:17,960
He's quite a pig. He's long and he's smooth, said Zuckerman.

74
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:27,399
That's right, agreed Lurvy. He's as smooth as they come. He's some pig.

75
00:07:27,399 --> 00:07:32,198
When Mr. Zuckerman got back to the house. He took off his workclo and put

76
00:07:32,198 --> 00:07:37,880
on his best suit. Then he got into his car and drove to the minister's house.

77
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:42,760
He stayed for an hour and explained to the minister that a miracle had happened

78
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:48,439
on the farm. So far, said Zuckerman, only four people on earth know about

79
00:07:48,439 --> 00:07:56,359
this miracle. Myself, my wife, Edith, my hired man, Lurvy, and you.

80
00:07:56,359 --> 00:08:01,639
Don't tell anybody else, said the minister. We don't know what it means

81
00:08:01,639 --> 00:08:07,399
yet, but uh perhaps if I give thought to it, I can explain it in my sermon next

82
00:08:07,399 --> 00:08:14,439
Sunday. There can be no doubt that you have a most unusual pig. I intend to

83
00:08:14,439 --> 00:08:19,238
speak about it in my sermon and point out the fact that this community has

84
00:08:19,238 --> 00:08:22,439
been visited with a wondrous animal.

85
00:08:22,439 --> 00:08:27,960
By the way, does this pig have a name?

86
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:34,359
Why yes, said Mr. Zuckerman. My little niece calls him Wilbur. She's a rather

87
00:08:34,359 --> 00:08:40,118
queer child, full of notions. She raised the pig on a bottle, and I bought him

88
00:08:40,118 --> 00:08:46,039
from her when he was a month old. He shook hands with the minister and left.

89
00:08:46,039 --> 00:08:55,880
Secrets are hard to keep. Long before Sunday came, the news spread all over the county.

90
00:08:55,880 --> 00:09:00,599
Everybody knew that a sign had appeared in a spider's web on the Zuckerman

91
00:09:00,599 --> 00:09:06,439
place. Everybody knew that the Zuckermanman's had a wondrous pig.

92
00:09:06,439 --> 00:09:11,319
People came from miles around to look at Wilbur and to read the words on

93
00:09:11,319 --> 00:09:20,439
Charlotte's Web. The Zuckerman's driveway was full of cars and trucks from morning till night.

94
00:09:20,439 --> 00:09:27,399
Fords and Chevys and Buick Roadmasters and GMC pickups and Plymouths and

95
00:09:27,399 --> 00:09:33,238
Studebakers and Packards and Doodtos with gyroatic transmissions and

96
00:09:33,238 --> 00:09:40,279
osmobiles with rocket engines and Jeep station wagons and Pontiacs.

97
00:09:40,279 --> 00:09:46,039
The news of the wonderful pig spread clear up into the hills, and farmers

98
00:09:46,039 --> 00:09:51,560
came rattling down in buggies and buck boards to stand hour after hour at

99
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:58,599
Wilbur's pin, admiring the miraculous animal. All said they had never seen

100
00:09:58,599 --> 00:10:03,079
such a pig before in their lives.

101
00:10:03,079 --> 00:10:08,039
When Fern told her mother that Avery had tried to hit the Zuckerman spider with a

102
00:10:08,039 --> 00:10:13,880
stick, Mrs. Arable was so shocked that she sent Avery to bed without any supper

103
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:19,079
as punishment. In the days that followed, Mr. Zuckerman was so busy

104
00:10:19,079 --> 00:10:24,359
entertaining visitors that he neglected his farmwork. He wore his good clothes

105
00:10:24,359 --> 00:10:30,279
all the time now, got right into them when he got up in the morning.

106
00:10:30,279 --> 00:10:35,560
Mrs. Zuckerman prepared special meals for Wilbur. Lurvy shaved and got a

107
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:41,238
haircut, and his principal farm duty was to feed the pig while people looked on.

108
00:10:41,238 --> 00:10:46,359
Mr. Zuckerman ordered Lurvy to increase Wilbur's feedings from three meals a day

109
00:10:46,359 --> 00:10:51,639
to four meals a day. The Zuckermanmans were so busy with visitors, they forgot

110
00:10:51,639 --> 00:10:56,520
about other things on the farm. The blackberries got ripe, and Mrs.

111
00:10:56,520 --> 00:11:01,479
Zuckerman failed to put up any blackberry jam. The corn needed hoing

112
00:11:01,479 --> 00:11:06,118
and Lurvy didn't find time to hoe it.

113
00:11:06,118 --> 00:11:13,880
On Sunday, the church was full. The minister explained the miracle. He said

114
00:11:13,880 --> 00:11:19,000
that the words on the spider's web proved that human beings must always be

115
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:23,639
on the watch for the coming of wonders.

116
00:11:23,639 --> 00:11:29,399
All in all, the Zuckermanman's pig pin was the center of attraction. Fern was

117
00:11:29,399 --> 00:11:34,039
happy, for she felt that Charlotte's trick was working and that Wilbur's life

118
00:11:34,039 --> 00:11:39,880
would be saved. But she found that the barn was not nearly as pleasant. Too

119
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:48,639
many people. She liked it better when she could be all alone with her friends, the animals.

120
00:11:51,079 --> 00:11:56,238
Chapter 12. A meeting.
